## 5. Compliance

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion | Status (2026-07-07) |
|----|-------------|-------------------|---------------------|
| CXC-FL-C1 | Graph renders wiring | A design's bindings render as widget↔namespace wires; namespaces are hub nodes | PASS — build_graph projects subscribe/attr/behavior/publish rows; golden `flow_mode_chrome` pins the chrome |
| CXC-FL-C2 | Synced projection | A wire drawn in Flow writes the binding; Layout/Bindings/Source reflect it; raw-spec fidelity holds | PASS — simplest CXC-BIND form into the RAW spec; Bindings rows + Source text asserted; export round-trips byte-identical incl. `external:`; bare-string-visible command-path fix found+closed |
| CXC-FL-C3 | Layout↔Flow toggle | The WW toggles between pixel layout and the node graph on the same design | PASS — `composer/ww/mode` bus state (buttons + Intelligence); WC follows the lens |
| CXC-FL-C4 | Live discovery | An external namespace from another bus participant appears in the Bus·Live rail within one poll | PASS — MQTT smoke: a separate ComposeApp peer's undeclared namespaces appear live w/ engine (peer) + value + source, both platforms |
| CXC-FL-C5 | Filter (P0) | keyword + prefix-glob + category filters narrow a 60+ namespace rail; "N of M" reflects it | PASS — 62-namespace rail → `jumpdrive/*` = 3 of 62; substring + categories + emergent prefix chips |
| CXC-FL-C6 | Discover-and-wire | Dragging a live namespace onto the canvas authors a subscription binding | PASS — real pointer path tested (rail row → expanded attr port; open-canvas drop = declare/subscribe); namespace auto-declared external w/ observed engine |
| CXC-FL-C7 | Declare-expected | Binding to a not-yet-live namespace activates when it first publishes | PASS — "+ listen" affordance declares; previewed widget follows the FIRST publish; kind flips expected → subscribed-external |
| CXC-FL-C8 | Pattern subscription | A widget bound to `jumpdrive/*` receives every matching namespace, incl. ones appearing later | PASS — bus, engine, WW preview, and real-MQTT tiers; later-created members verified at each |
| CXC-FL-C9 | Intelligence parity | An Intelligence wiring/subscribing over the bus produces the identical graph + bindings | PASS — identical node/wire sets + byte-equal YAML from pure bus commands; `bus_live` added to the state snapshot so a peer sees the rail |

